                    r2_briefing:        `Day 12, 1:14 PM. Carolina Restrepo at Andes Capital Partners circulates an analyst note calling Helio Verde "rudderless" and the new CEO "without a strategy." The chair Manuel Beltran-Rojas calls. Three minutes. He tells Lucia he is not asking her to capitulate — he is asking her to decide whether her silence is a strategy or a stall, and to defend the decision in 72 hours.<br><br><b>Decision.</b> How do you respond to the Restrepo note and the chair's call — with a public vision statement, with continued silence and no defense, or by deflecting publicly while privately defending the diagnostic phase to Manuel as a research design?`,
                    r2_posture_title:   `The Restrepo Note · The Chair's 72-Hour Window`,
                    r2_posture_hint:    `Gerstner: the last thing the company needs right now is a vision. The defensible answer is not silence — it is silence with a defended diagnostic-phase warrant.`,
                    r2_o1:              `Respond to Restrepo with a public vision speech reaffirming the predecessor strategic priorities`,
                    r2_o2:              `Stay silent — no defense to Manuel, no public statement, hope the noise passes`,
                    r2_o3:              `Deflect publicly — defend the diagnostic phase to Manuel as research design with named outputs by Day 100`,

                    r3_context:         `Day 21–30 · The 12% target pressure · La Sabana plant week`,
                    r3_briefing:        `The predecessor stretch growth target is 12% organic revenue. Three of the cabinet members ask Lucia, in separate one-on-ones, whether she will reaffirm it at the all-employee town hall. The CFO seat is still vacant. Lucia has not yet visited the La Sabana plant. The plant manager, Esteban Quiros Vega, is on the schedule for Day 19.<br><br><b>Decision.</b> What is your stance on the 12% growth target during the diagnostic phase?`,
                    r3_posture_title:   `The 12% Target — Reaffirm, Reject, or Defer?`,
                    r3_posture_hint:    `Premature commitment is the modal failure mode. Premature de-commitment is its mirror. Watkins discipline is to defer with a date — not to decide yet, but to defend the deferral.`,
                    r3_o1:              `Reaffirm the 12% target publicly — show analysts and the cabinet that the new CEO is committed`,
                    r3_o2:              `Publicly reject the target as unattainable — pre-empt the activist note`,
                    r3_o3:              `Defer the decision to Day 130 with a public commitment to revisit it against the capacity arithmetic`,

                    r4_context:         `Day 31–40 · La Sabana visit · The 11-minute conversation · THE LINE`,
                    r4_briefing:        `On Day 19, on her way back from La Sabana, Lucia detoured eleven minutes through the production floor with Esteban Quiros. Quiros reframed the diagnostic — the binding constraint is not the SAP transformation, it is the production line itself, configured fourteen years ago for traditional-trade SKU stability. Doña Carmen Iturbide had asked Lucia which one operational number, if it changed by 30%, would change every other number in the P&L. The cabinet does not know this conversation happened.<br><br><b>Decision.</b> What do you do with the Quiros insight?`,
                    r4_posture_title:   `The Quiros Insight — Pivot, Ignore, or Triangulate?`,
                    r4_posture_hint:    `The CEO who decrees on a one-source insight is captured by the source. The CEO who ignores ground-truth that contradicts the cabinet narrative is captured by the cabinet. Triangulation is the diagnostic-phase discipline.`,
                    r4_o1:              `Pivot publicly — declare changeover capability the binding constraint at Friday cabinet meeting`,
                    r4_o2:              `Ignore the conversation — the cabinet narrative on SAP is more sophisticated than one plant manager`,
                    r4_o3:              `Triangulate quietly — commission the shadow audit to test the changeover hypothesis against the SAP narrative`,

                    r5_context:         `Day 41–50 · The SAP transformation cabinet workshop`,
                    r5_briefing:        `Renata Coralles and the interim CFO present an accelerated SAP transformation case at the Wednesday cabinet workshop. USD 24M over 18 months, decisive, the cabinet narrative made operational. The shadow audit interim has not yet landed. The Quiros hypothesis has not yet been tested across the other plants. Renata says, in plain language, that the cabinet needs to know whether Lucia is going to support the program.<br><br><b>Decision.</b> What is your stance on SAP acceleration in week 7?`,
                    r5_posture_title:   `SAP Acceleration — Approve, Cancel, or Defer?`,
                    r5_posture_hint:    `Approving cabinet capital before the shadow audit returns is cabinet capture. Cancelling a multi-year program in week 7 without warrant is decree-style action. The disciplined posture defers and pairs the deferral with a date.`,
                    r5_o1:              `Approve the SAP acceleration — back the cabinet, settle the question, ship the capital`,
                    r5_o2:              `Cancel the SAP program — the binding constraint is capacity, not technology`,
                    r5_o3:              `Defer the SAP timeline pending the capacity case at Day 180`,

                    r6_context:         `Day 51–60 · The town hall demand · Restrepo's follow-up note`,
                    r6_briefing:        `Beatriz Solis, the CHRO, urges Lucia to schedule an all-employee town hall before Day 60. She argues the silence is being read inside the company as indecision. On the same week, Restrepo publishes a sharper follow-up — Helio Verde is losing share in the modern-retail channel that is growing, and two Brazilian competitors are investing behind capacity reconfiguration. Tomas asks whether Lucia wants to brief the cabinet on the follow-up before any public response.<br><br><b>Decision.</b> What format do you choose for organizational communication in week 8?`,
                    r6_posture_title:   `Town Hall Format — Vision, Skip, or Listening Summary?`,
                    r6_posture_hint:    `Nadella deflected three explicit press requests for "the new strategy" in his first 90 days. The Day-30 listening summary is the canonical pattern — a "what I have heard so far" message, not a "this is the strategy" message.`,
