                    r10_context:        `Day 88–100 · The 100-day memo · Camila Brenes fifteen seconds`,
                    r10_briefing:       `It is Day 87. Forty-seven conversations, five site visits, two trips to Mexico, the shadow audit, three cabinet workshops. Camila Brenes, a junior brand manager, passes Lucia in the hallway and thanks her, in fifteen seconds, for not announcing a strategy. Manuel will receive the memo on Day 102 at the regular board meeting. The memo is the artifact that closes the diagnostic phase and earns the autonomy of the operational phase.<br><br><b>Decision.</b> What kind of memo do you write?`,
                    r10_posture_title:  `The 100-Day Memo to the Chair`,
                    r10_posture_hint:   `Gerstner discipline — refuse to over-commit on what has not been earned. Watkins five-paragraph template — concluded, not concluded with dates, three bets, cadence, restraint. Manuel has heard a vision speech from every prior CEO. He wants the diagnostic.`,
